==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|fled}}
* {{l|ang|flett}} 

===Etymology1===
From {{proto|Germanic|flajan|floor|lang=en}} from {{proto|Germanic|flataz|flat|lang=en}} from {{proto|Indo-European|plat-|flat|lang=en}}. Akin to {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|flet|flet, flette|lang=ofs}} "dwelling, house".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/flet/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=n|pl=flet}}

# the [[floor]], [[ground]]
#: ''Heó on '''flet''' gecrong'' &mdash; She sank to the ground.
# a [[dwelling]], [[habitation]], [[house]], [[cottage]], [[hall]]
#: ''Gif ðæt '''flet''' geblódgad wyrþe.'' &mdash; If the house be stained with blood.

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-a-n|flet}}

====Derived terms====
* [[fletræst]] f. — couch
* [[fletsittend]] m. — sitter in hall, courtier, guest.
* [[fletwerod]] n. — hall-troop, body-guard

====Descendants====
* English [[flat]]

===Etymology2===
Likely from {{proto|Germanic|flutōnan|to float|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|pleud-||plew-||plōw-|to float, swim, fly|lang=en}}; compare {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|fløde||cream|lang=da}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|fleytið||skimming|lang=is}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|fløte||cream|lang=no}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|flete}}
* {{l|ang|fliet}}
* {{l|ang|flyte}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|g=f|head=flēt|pl=flēta}}

# [[cream]], [[skimming]], [[curds]]
#: ''Hwít sealt dó on reám oððe góde '''fléte'''. &mdash; Put white salt into cream or good skimmings.

